WEBVTT

00:00:02.947 --> 00:00:03.706
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 1

00:00:04.644 --> 00:00:07.040
<v><b>A:</b></v> This is for my foodie friends.

00:00:07.468 --> 00:00:10.789
In case you thought lettuce was only for salads,

00:00:11.107 --> 00:00:14.381
here I’m cooking it in some butter with an onion.

00:00:14.785 --> 00:00:19.524
Then I add some mushrooms, chicken, fresh tomatoes,

00:00:19.549 --> 00:00:22.238
and some other things – not sure yet.

00:00:22.388 --> 00:00:28.915
Lettuce is also great in soups, or you can grill it and serve it with blue cheese.

00:00:30.793 --> 00:00:31.542
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 2

00:00:32.466 --> 00:00:35.557
<v><b>B:</b></v> We didn’t feel like cooking last night, and besides,

00:00:35.582 --> 00:00:37.903
we didn’t have any food in the house,

00:00:38.182 --> 00:00:43.868
so we decided to order some take-out salads from our wonderful local pizzeria.

00:00:44.555 --> 00:00:49.557
They were all very good, but my favorite was a chicken salad

00:00:49.582 --> 00:00:56.260
with carrots, tomatoes, peppers, lettuce, and some pieces of fried bread.

00:00:57.903 --> 00:00:58.663
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 3

00:00:59.585 --> 00:01:04.585
<v><b>C:</b></v> Brunch, Sunday afternoon, at a restaurant in the East Village, called Timna.

00:01:05.034 --> 00:01:07.563
We had lots of different sharing plates.

00:01:07.865 --> 00:01:13.928
I loved everything, especially this dish called <i>shakshuka</i>, which is North African,

00:01:14.162 --> 00:01:17.127
and it’s basically eggs in a tomato sauce,

00:01:17.338 --> 00:01:21.132
but the mixture of herbs and spices makes it taste great.

00:01:21.521 --> 00:01:25.262
And the bread we had to dip in the sauce was wonderful, too.

00:01:25.543 --> 00:01:27.415
Go there. Soon.

00:01:28.951 --> 00:01:29.758
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 4

00:01:30.534 --> 00:01:32.740
<v><b>D:</b></v> OK, guys, this is it!

00:01:33.199 --> 00:01:38.128
Our Thanksgiving dinner – which we had at 6:30 last night.

00:01:38.798 --> 00:01:45.596
All the usual things: turkey with cranberry sauce, mashed potatoes,

00:01:45.810 --> 00:01:52.830
sweet potatoes, lots of vegetables, and more… and more…

00:01:53.900 --> 00:01:59.461
We thought about going to a restaurant this year, maybe having seafood,

00:02:00.052 --> 00:02:05.680
but then we decided, no, we like homemade and traditional,

00:02:06.205 --> 00:02:09.216
so we stayed at home and cooked together.

00:02:10.157 --> 00:02:16.633
I now need to spend a few hours on the sofa before I even think of going to bed.

00:02:17.385 --> 00:02:19.006
So, how was yours?